geojson-processed/

# Geodata. Only the pipeline's *inputs* are tracked: Data/JSon-Provinces-Orig is
# the province GeoJSON everything else is derived from, so it is source in all
# but name and worth a history. Everything beside it is an intermediate or an
# output the UI_* tools rewrite constantly, or the ~7 GB Canada120m.tif — none of
# which belongs in the repo. Keep those backed up by other means; git is not that.
#
# This must be ``Data/*`` and not ``Data/``: git cannot re-include anything
# inside an excluded *directory*, so the directory itself has to stay visible and
# its contents be excluded one level down for the negation below to take effect.
Data/*
!Data/JSon-Provinces-Orig/
unused/

# Claude Code: the shared project settings are tracked, the per-machine ones
# (paths, one-off tool approvals) are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine half of the project config: the screen calibration, and anything
# else true of one desk rather than of the project. Measured against particular
# monitors, so it is not merely useless on another machine but actively wrong.
# project_config.json — the project's own magic numbers — IS tracked.
project_config.local.json
.screen_ruler_config.json

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
